Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: When are representations and warranties required to be made according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: At Closing Only\nOption B: At Signing & At Closing\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 8.1 Conditions to Obligations of Acquirer to Effect the Merger. The obligations of Acquirer to effect the Merger are, in addition to the conditions set forth in Section 8.0, further subject to the satisfaction or (to the extent not prohibited by Law) waiver by Acquirer at or prior to the Effective Time of the following conditions: (a) each of the representations and warranties of the Target contained in this Agreement, without giving effect to any materiality or "Target Material Adverse Effect" or similar qualifications therein, shall be true and correct as of the Closing Date, except for such failures to be true and correct as would not, individually or in the aggregate, have a Target Material Adverse Effect, and (b) the representations and warranties that are expressly made as of a specific date shall be true and correct as of such specific date only, while those not made as of a specific date shall be true and correct both as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date. (Page 72)
